; offline-voice-gaps-band.bml — the gap register's grader, fkwu-witnessed (observe/offline-voice-gaps-run.bml).
;
; The door is spawned over gaps files and fixture ledgers this band writes under a scratch directory it makes and removes (stdin: gaps,
; root, walk, register, now_ms, zone_ms), so no live ledger is read and no live register row lands. Every shape is proven over fixture rows
; that read closed, open and unread. Then the band asks of every LIVING row of learn/offline-voice-gaps.jsonl: what would make this read closed
; while the thing is false? It runs the living rows over two fixture worlds, each a small git repository whose origin/main the door reads:
; a TRUE world, where each thing is so, and every row must read closed (no row is out of reach by construction); and a FALSE world, where each
; thing is false and looks true, and no row may read closed. A row added to the living file with no answer in the false world reads closed there and
; this band falls.
;
; Expected: 2097151
; Verdict 2097151 when every claim lands:
;   1    last: the last row's field against a threshold reads closed; against another field of the row reads open; `also` short reads open; `show` prints
;   2    unread, never closed: a field absent, no row holding `where`, a source absent, a kind with no reader, and a comparison strings do not know
;   4    where tests: {">":0} {"in":[..]} {"absent":1} {"!=":v} {"present":1} and an equality each choose the row; within_ms stale reads open; on_slot off every slot reads open;
;        none_reads open reads open; not_in reads open when the row's value stands in that source
;   8    share: the permille of rows holding `match` among the rows holding `where`: 500 pm reads open, 1000 pm closed; since_ms reads only the rows at
;        or after it; a seam no counted row holds reads unread; within_ms reads only rows that young, so a lane gone quiet reads open and a miss ages out
;   16   table: two cells of a markdown table compared as decimals in milli, the last row of each key; a missing key is unread
;   32   schedule: at a fixed instant 21 slots are due, first and last named; a stamp and a landed row read their slots; a row only in the working tree,
;        a walk-here row, a rented row, a session row and another door's stamp read nothing; a retry row is a note, never a reading; no walk checkout is unread
;   64   the summary counts, one register row per run with the counts and each gap's verdict, exit 0
;   128  a missing gaps file is refused by name, exit non-zero, no register row
;   256  the living rows over the true world: every row reads closed
;   512  the living rows over the false world: no row reads closed, though a session's draft, child and judgment stand answered inside a slot's window (by_schedule).
;        And over the true world eight days later, when every door stopped: only the rows that read a record or a thirty-day window may still read closed
;   1024 landings told native: over the true world every source-changing landing; over the false world none: a subject with no crossings row, a co-author's
;        signature, a crossings row a rented mind coordinated
;   2048 gaps: closed natively only with a green real option on the schedule, a native landing touching its writable paths, and no guide row
;   4096 session-share: the query and voice rows read the schedule's and the person's rows only, naming their counts: a session's miss and a measurement arm's miss in the true world do not move the share
;   8192 stood: a native landing older than seven days counts when its lines stand and a gate reads them; the wrong line a later commit repaired and a landing no gate reads are held out by name, a young landing waits
;   16384 thin: Q4 against Q8 reads the schedule's local-run rows and a side gone quiet reads open; plan reads rows a native landing carried; guided, last-option and self-turn read the voice's rungs, and a no-model rung's green row moves only self-rung
;   32768 rent: rented tokens per week is each session's growth inside the window, so a long-lived session's earlier tokens do not count and its new ones do; a meter gone quiet reads open; a row whose usage did not read never closes the week, and rent that did read still opens it
;   65536 steer: each open row whose next names a band is offered, queue when that band stands and finding when it does not; a row with no next is not offered; the share is read; the queue stays unwritten; an absent register is refused
;   131072 exam: a kind reads closed only from rows a native landing added, denied, answered and graded: a session's row, an undenied row, an unanswered one and an ungraded one each hold it open; a first held-out reading short stays short after a later full one;
;        the exam's own fixture plan is no plan of the body's
;   262144 scope: a query-scope line reads open with what answers there, closed only when the person said, unread when no line names it or its state is neither
;   524288 truth: the living rows over a world a native landing carried, each row false by the hollowness it must refuse: a plan the voice replied to and
;        no planner verified; a prose answer with no session column, named unattributed; a prose answer from a detached line, named
;        detached; the 27B child better by 13 among siblings scattered 61; one 3B child
;        alone; a reading of the voice's with nothing generated; rows re-read from voice readings that stopped moving nine days ago; a heal that returned
;        nothing; E4 holding with no support read; a steer ledger absent, its writer named. None reads closed
;   1048576 held-out: the living held-out row names a sealed set, the scenarios it holds and the prompt it was sealed under, and two worlds of its own read it: the set
;        read whole under the prompt it was sealed under reads open (no row counts); read under another prompt after a no-prompt arm, a grounded arm, an adapter arm and
;        a cut reading of it, it reads closed by its first whole reading of the voice as it speaks, which a later short one never replaces
; preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/bml/live.bml form-stdlib/bml/host-child.bml form-stdlib/bml/exit-proof.bml
section [form.bml] {
 class OfflineVoiceGapsBand {
  def ovb-dir() = ".hearth/offline-voice-gaps-band";
  def ovb-fx() = ovb-dir() ++ "/fx";
  def ovb-walk() = ovb-fx() ++ "/walk";
  def ovb-register() = ovb-dir() ++ "/register.jsonl";
  def ovb-has?(hay, needle) = str_find(hay, needle, 0) >= 0;
  // 2026-10-31 15:25:00 at +08:00: every slot and every window below is read from this instant
  def ovb-now() = 1793431500000;
  def ovb-zone() = 28800000;
  def ovb-hour() = 3600000;
  def ovb-day() = 86400000;
  // ---- the fixtures: one ledger per shape, each with rows that read closed, open and unread ----------------------------
  def ovb-gap(id, kind, rest) = "{\"id\":\"" ++ id ++ "\",\"title\":\"t-" ++ id ++ "\",\"kind\":\"" ++ kind ++ "\",\"goal\":\"g-" ++ id ++ "\"," ++ rest ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-gaps() = ovb-gap("g-closed", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"flow.jsonl\",\"field\":\"open_gaps\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0,\"show\":[\"gap\"]")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-open", "readings", "\"source\":\"align.jsonl\",\"field\":\"predicates_passed\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"against\":\"predicates_total\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-also", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"flow.jsonl\",\"field\":\"open_gaps\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0,\"also\":[{\"field\":\"gaps_unread\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0}]")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-nofield", "readings", "\"source\":\"nofield.jsonl\",\"field\":\"open_gaps\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-nowhere", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"turn.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"dry\":0},\"field\":\"band_green\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-absent", "lora", "\"source\":\"absent.jsonl\",\"field\":\"remote_dependence\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":\"none\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-share-open", "coverage", "\"source\":\"cov.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"lookup\"},\"match\":{\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-share-closed", "voice-availability", "\"source\":\"cov.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"plan\"},\"match\":{\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-share-since", "voice-availability", "\"source\":\"cov.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"lookup\"},\"since_ms\":10,\"match\":{\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-seam", "coverage", "\"source\":\"cov.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"plan\"},\"match\":{\"answered\":1},\"seam\":{\"source\":\"form-find\"},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-share-stale", "coverage", "\"source\":\"cov-old.jsonl\",\"within_ms\":1000,\"none_reads\":\"open\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"plan\"},\"match\":{\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-share-window", "coverage", "\"source\":\"cov-old.jsonl\",\"within_ms\":1000,\"none_reads\":\"open\",\"where\":{\"kind\":\"lookup\"},\"match\":{\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0},\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-table-open", "plan-doc", "\"source\":\"plan.md\",\"row_key\":\"Q4_K_M\",\"against_key\":\"Q8_0\",\"column\":9,\"compare\":\">=\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-table-closed", "plan-doc", "\"source\":\"plan.md\",\"row_key\":\"Q8_0\",\"against_key\":\"Q4_K_M\",\"column\":9,\"compare\":\">=\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-table-nokey", "plan-doc", "\"source\":\"plan.md\",\"row_key\":\"Q2_K\",\"against_key\":\"Q8_0\",\"column\":9,\"compare\":\">=\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-kind", "moon", "\"source\":\"flow.jsonl\",\"field\":\"open_gaps\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-strop", "lora", "\"source\":\"strop.jsonl\",\"field\":\"class\",\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":\"begun\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-test-gt", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"tests.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"option\":{\">\":0}},\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":2")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-test-in", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"tests.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"lane\":{\"in\":[\"a\",\"c\"]}},\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-test-absent", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"tests.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"session\":{\"absent\":1}},\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":2")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-test-ne", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"tests.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"readers\":{\"!=\":\"native-voice\"}},\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":2")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-test-present", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"tests.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"readers\":{\"present\":1}},\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":3")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-within", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"flow.jsonl\",\"field\":\"open_gaps\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":0,\"within_ms\":1000")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-none-open", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"turn.jsonl\",\"where\":{\"dry\":0},\"field\":\"band_green\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1,\"none_reads\":\"open\"")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-not-in", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"guided.jsonl\",\"field\":\"band_green\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1,\"not_in\":{\"source\":\"guide.jsonl\",\"on\":\"gap\"}")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-off-slot", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"slotted-off.jsonl\",\"on_slot\":1,\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-on-slot", "turn-ledger", "\"source\":\"slotted-on.jsonl\",\"on_slot\":1,\"field\":\"mark\",\"compare\":\"==\",\"threshold\":1")
   ++ ovb-gap("g-slots", "walk-schedule", "\"source\":\".hearth/walk.began\",\"checkout\":\"walk\",\"days\":7,\"grace_ms\":2700000,\"stamp_within_ms\":2700000,\"compare\":\">=\",\"threshold\":1000");
  def ovb-plan() = "# a plan\n\n| quant | run | wall ms | a | b | c | d | e | f | decode tok/s | g |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Q4_K_M | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0.55 | 1 |\n| Q4_K_M | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0.61 | 1 |\n| Q8_0 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2.13 | 1 |\n| Q8_0 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2.79 | 1 |\n\nprose after the table\n";
  def ovb-write(root, path, text) {
   let made = hch-mkdirs(ep-dir-of(root ++ "/" ++ path));
   write_file_text(root ++ "/" ++ path, text);
  }
  def ep-dir-of(p) { let at = ep-rfind(p, "/", 0, -1); at < 0 ? "." : substring(p, 0, at); }
  def ovb-write-fixtures() {
   let a = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "gaps.jsonl", ovb-gaps());
   let b = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "flow.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":1,\"open_gaps\":2}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":2,\"open_gaps\":0,\"gaps_unread\":8,\"gap\":\"g9\"}\n");
   let c = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "align.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":3,\"predicates_passed\":87,\"predicates_total\":93}\n");
   let d = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "nofield.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":4,\"other\":1}\n");
   let e = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "turn.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":5,\"dry\":1,\"band_green\":1}\n");
   let f = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "cov.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":11,\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":12,\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":1,\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":5}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":2,\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":0,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"kind\":\"plan\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"kind\":\"plan\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n");
   let g = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "plan.md", ovb-plan());
   let h = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "strop.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":8,\"class\":\"begun\"}\n");
   let i = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "tests.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":1,\"option\":0,\"lane\":\"a\",\"session\":\"s\",\"readers\":\"native-voice\",\"mark\":1}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":2,\"option\":1,\"lane\":\"b\",\"mark\":2}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":3,\"option\":0,\"lane\":\"b\",\"session\":\"s\",\"readers\":\"native-voice\",\"mark\":3}\n");
   let j = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "guided.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":9,\"gap\":\"g7\",\"band_green\":1}\n");
   let k = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "guide.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":9,\"gap\":\"g7\"}\n");
   let k2 = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "slotted-off.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ ovb-ago(3).str() ++ ",\"mark\":1}\n");
   let k3 = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "slotted-on.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ ovb-ago(1).str() ++ ",\"mark\":1}\n");
   // plan answered long ago and nothing since; lookup missed long ago and answers now
   let k4 = ovb-write(ovb-fx(), "cov-old.jsonl", "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ (ovb-now() - 5000).str() ++ ",\"kind\":\"plan\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ (ovb-now() - 5000).str() ++ ",\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":0,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ (ovb-now() - 10).str() ++ ",\"kind\":\"lookup\",\"answered\":1,\"rent_tokens\":0}\n");
   ovb-write-slots-world();
  }
  // ---- git, for the worlds --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def ovb-git(root, step, args) = hch-run-quiet-in(ovb-dir() ++ "/io", "git-" ++ step, append(["git", "-C", root, "-c", "user.name=band", "-c", "user.email=band@local", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false"], args), "", hch-by(120000));
  def ovb-init(root) {
   let i = ovb-git(root, "init", ["init", "-q", "."]);
   0;
  }
  def ovb-commit-at(root, subject, body, paths, at) {
   let added = ovb-git(root, "add", append(["add", "-f", "--"], paths));
   let msg = (String) body == "" ? subject : subject ++ "\n\n" ++ body;
   ovb-git(root, "commit", ["commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "--date=" ++ (at / 1000).str() ++ " +0800", "-m", msg]);
  }
  def ovb-commit(root, subject, body, paths) = ovb-commit-at(root, subject, body, paths, ovb-now());
  // a day's last slot, k days ago, and the landing subject its crossings row would name
  def ovb-old-slot(k) = ep-due-slots(ovb-now() - k * ovb-day(), ovb-zone(), 1, 2700000)[-1];
  def ovb-old-subject(s) = "Native turn " ++ hw-day-in(ovb-zone(), s[0]) ++ " " ++ ovb-hhmm(s) ++ ": the body's own loop, no rented mind";
  def ovb-publish(root) = ovb-git(root, "ref", ["update-ref", "refs/remotes/origin/main", "HEAD"]);
  // ---- a crossings row, a slot's name --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def ovb-crossing(at, m, by, exe, rented, extra) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"movement\":\"" ++ m ++ "\",\"coordinated_by\":\"" ++ by ++ "\",\"coordinator\":\"" ++ exe ++ "\",\"rented_mind\":" ++ rented.str() ++ ",\"coordinating_rent\":0" ++ extra ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-kept(at, m) = ovb-crossing(at, m, "host-schedule", "/sbin/launchd", 0, "");
  def ovb-hhmm(s) = substring(s[3], 0, 2) ++ substring(s[3], 3, 5);
  def ovb-slot-movement(s) = (String) s[1] == "scheduled-walk" ? "scheduled " ++ hw-day-in(ovb-zone(), s[0]) : "native-turn " ++ hw-day-in(ovb-zone(), s[0]) ++ " " ++ ovb-hhmm(s);
  def ovb-due() = ep-due-slots(ovb-now(), ovb-zone(), 7, 2700000);
  // the slots world, read by g-slots: 21 slots due, and every way a row can look like it read one
  def ovb-write-slots-world() {
   let due = ovb-due();
   let walk = ovb-walk();
   // the last slot (12:30 today) reads a stamp and no row; the last night's is a landed row; the rest stay unread
   let night = foldl((best, s) => (String) s[1] == "scheduled-walk" ? s : best, [], due);
   let landedRow = ovb-kept(night[0] + 60000, ovb-slot-movement(night));
   let wrongs = ovb-crossing(due[0][0] + 60000, "walk-here " ++ hw-day-in(ovb-zone(), due[0][0]), "host-schedule", "/sbin/launchd", 0, "") ++ ovb-crossing(due[1][0] + 60000, ovb-slot-movement(due[1]), "session", "/bin/zsh", 1, "") ++ ovb-crossing(due[2][0] + 60000, ovb-slot-movement(due[2]), "host-schedule", "/sbin/launchd", 0, ",\"session\":\"s\"") ++ ovb-crossing(due[3][0] + 60000, ovb-slot-movement(due[3]), "host-schedule", "/bin/zsh", 0, "");
   let wrote = ovb-write(walk, "receipts/crossings-ledger.jsonl", wrongs ++ landedRow);
   let i = ovb-init(walk);
   let c = ovb-commit(walk, "world", "", ["receipts/crossings-ledger.jsonl"]);
   let p = ovb-publish(walk);
   // a row only in the working tree reads nothing: it lands after the ref was published
   let inTree = ovb-write(walk, "receipts/crossings-ledger.jsonl", wrongs ++ landedRow ++ ovb-kept(due[4][0] + 60000, ovb-slot-movement(due[4])));
   let last = due[-1];
   let stamp = "pid=7 at=" ++ (last[0] + 30000).str() ++ " door=" ++ last[1] ++ "\npid=8 at=" ++ (due[5][0] + 30000).str() ++ " door=" ++ (String) ((String) due[5][1] == "day-turn" ? "scheduled-walk" : "day-turn") ++ "\n";
   let s = ovb-write(walk, ".hearth/walk.began", stamp);
   ovb-write(walk, ".hearth/walk-retry.jsonl", "{\"phase\":\"outcome\",\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ (due[6][0] + 600000).str() ++ ",\"door\":\"" ++ due[6][1] ++ "\",\"slot\":\"" ++ due[6][3] ++ "\",\"class\":\"begun\"}\n");
  }
  // ---- the living rows' two worlds ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def ovb-true() = ovb-dir() ++ "/true";
  def ovb-false() = ovb-dir() ++ "/false";
  def ovb-ago(h) = ovb-now() - h * ovb-hour();
  def ovb-turn-row(gap, at, option, green, rest) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"gap\":\"" ++ gap ++ "\",\"option\":" ++ option.str() ++ ",\"band_green\":" ++ green.str() ++ ",\"dry\":0,\"test\":0,\"coordinated_by\":\"host-schedule\",\"coordinator\":\"/sbin/launchd\",\"remote_dependence\":\"none\",\"rung\":\"first\",\"band_after\":1,\"lane_reason\":\"\",\"lane_status\":\"complete\"" ++ rest ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-scenario(id) = "{\"id\":\"" ++ id ++ "\",\"predicates\":[\"a\"]}\n";
  def ovb-tagged(id, axes) = "{\"id\":\"" ++ id ++ "\",\"axes\":[" ++ str-join-with(map(a => "\"" ++ a ++ "\"", axes), ",") ++ "]}\n";
  def ovb-set(s) = "model/fixtures/alignment/" ++ s;
  // a reading names its sets, its role and its adapter; so does each row of its axis ledger
  def ovb-reading(at, sets, scenarios, total, passed, role, adapter) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"model\":\"qwen38-q8\",\"prompt_digest\":\"d1\",\"fixtures\":\"" ++ sets ++ "\",\"scenarios\":" ++ scenarios.str() ++ ",\"predicates_total\":" ++ total.str() ++ ",\"predicates_passed\":" ++ passed.str() ++ ",\"role\":\"" ++ role ++ "\",\"adapter\":\"" ++ adapter ++ "\"}\n";
  def ovb-axis-row(at, sets, axis, total, passed, role, adapter) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"model\":\"qwen38-q8\",\"prompt_digest\":\"d1\",\"fixtures\":\"" ++ sets ++ "\",\"axis\":\"" ++ axis ++ "\",\"predicates_total\":" ++ total.str() ++ ",\"predicates_passed\":" ++ passed.str() ++ ",\"role\":\"" ++ role ++ "\",\"adapter\":\"" ++ adapter ++ "\"}\n";
  def ovb-all-axes() = ["core values", "protocols", "interfaces", "capabilities", "tone of voice", "core features", "core principles"];
  def ovb-axis-rows(at, sets, axes, total, passed, role, adapter) = foldl((acc, a) => acc ++ ovb-axis-row(at, sets, a, total, passed, role, adapter), "", axes);
  def ovb-cov-of(at, kind, source, answered, rent, session) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"kind\":\"" ++ kind ++ "\",\"source\":\"" ++ source ++ "\",\"lane\":\"l\",\"model\":\"\",\"answered\":" ++ answered.str() ++ ",\"rent_tokens\":" ++ rent.str() ++ ",\"wall_ms\":1,\"session\":\"" ++ session ++ "\"}\n";
  def ovb-cov(at, kind, source, answered, rent) = ovb-cov-of(at, kind, source, answered, rent, "");
  def ovb-voice() = ",\"local_generated_ids\":9";
  def ovb-no-model() = ",\"local_generated_ids\":0";
  def ovb-run-row(at, session, model, rate, rest) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"session\":\"" ++ session ++ "\",\"lane\":\"registry-weights\",\"status\":\"answered\",\"generated_ids\":9,\"model\":\"/m/" ++ model ++ ".gguf\",\"decode_tok_s\":" ++ rate ++ rest ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-meter(at, session, total) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"session\":\"" ++ session ++ "\",\"rented_total\":" ++ total.str() ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-lora(at, parent, reading, parentLoss, childLoss, better, rent, extra) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"parent\":\"form/form-stdlib/adapters/" ++ parent ++ "\",\"valid_reading\":\"" ++ reading ++ "\",\"parent_loss_milli\":" ++ parentLoss.str() ++ ",\"child_loss_milli\":" ++ childLoss.str() ++ ",\"better\":" ++ better.str() ++ ",\"rent_tokens\":" ++ rent.str() ++ ",\"train_rows\":8,\"steps\":20,\"valid_rows\":5" ++ extra ++ "}\n";
  def ovb-exit(at, word) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"E1\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E1_reading\":\"r\",\"E2\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E2_reading\":\"r\",\"E3\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E3_reading\":\"r\",\"E4\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E4_reading\":\"r\",\"E4_support\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E5\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E5_reading\":\"r\",\"E6\":\"" ++ word ++ "\",\"E6_reading\":\"r\"}\n";
  def ovb-doors() = ["observe/local-plan-run.bml", "observe/native-turn-run.bml", "observe/prompt-draft-run.bml", "observe/draft-native-reading-run.bml", "observe/draft-readings-to-rows.bml", "observe/lora-lift-run.bml", "observe/qwen-last-block-lift-run.bml", "observe/offline-exam-run.bml", "observe/local-flow-review.bml", "observe/self-steer-run.bml", "observe/self-distill-run.bml", "observe/self-review-run.bml"];
  // the exam's rows, and the held-out row's own where, read from the living row so a later set moves one line
  def ovb-exam-kinds() = ["prose", "lookup", "code", "plan", "structural"];
  def ovb-exam-row(at, kind, session, denied, answered, graded, rent) = "{\"at_unix_ms\":" ++ at.str() ++ ",\"session\":\"" ++ session ++ "\",\"network_denied\":" ++ denied.str() ++ ",\"kind\":\"" ++ kind ++ "\",\"exam\":\"e\",\"answered\":" ++ answered.str() ++ ",\"graded\":" ++ graded.str() ++ ",\"rent_tokens\":" ++ rent.str() ++ ",\"wall_ms\":1,\"status\":\"answered\",\"failed\":\"\"}\n";
